---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About · CoreWise Academy">
  <main>
    <p class="mono-label accent">About the Academy</p>
    <h1 class="display">A publication, not a feed.</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        CoreWise Academy is an editorial publication about working with AI. Every guide is an
        original synthesis, written from multiple sources, structured to teach. Never a transcript
        summary, never a repost. Guides are charted into five fixed constellations, each with three
        shelves: Broad for the naked eye, Practitioner for the telescope, Deep for the observatory.
        Empty shelves stay visible. That is the roadmap, honestly drawn.
      </p>

      <h2>The editorial bar</h2>
      <p>
        A video qualifies as a source only if the editor personally learned something from it. Not
        "found it", not "skimmed it": learned from it. Every guide credits its sources by creator,
        video, and timestamp, and quotes are short and attributed. Merging a guide into the atlas is
        an editorial act: nothing publishes without review.
      </p>

      <h2>Founder &amp; editor</h2>
      <p>
        CoreWise Academy is founded and edited by Ryan. There is no staff, no content team, no
        growth department. One editor, a strict bar, and an atlas that grows only as fast as real
        learning does.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>

  <style>
    main { max-width: calc(var(--measure) + 2 * var(--s-4)); margin: 0 auto; padding: var(--s-8) var(--s-4) var(--s-12); }
    h1 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, var(--text-3xl)); margin: var(--s-2) 0 var(--s-4); }
    .prose p { margin-bottom: var(--s-3); }
    .prose h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--text-xl); font-weight: 400; margin: var(--s-6) 0 var(--s-2); }
  </style>
</Base>
